        "fr-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "f23a9e37-c043-3571-b17a-aaf5ca1441f9",
                "word": "royauté",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "c40964a1-bf0d-4d35-b99e-3f4a422129d9",
                        "entry_id": "f23a9e37-c043-3571-b17a-aaf5ca1441f9",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "royautés"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "61c48a22-c138-3d94-91eb-3bd902df3cf3",
                        "entry_id": "f23a9e37-c043-3571-b17a-aaf5ca1441f9",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Régime, pouvoir, fonction d’un roi ou d’une reine."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "1c936d89-f0bf-4764-a82a-61487d009caf",
                                "sense_id": "61c48a22-c138-3d94-91eb-3bd902df3cf3",
                                "text": "Sur le continent, la lutte entre les diverses classes de la société, entre les communes et l’aristocratie, entre le serf et seigneur, appela bientôt la royauté à une nouvelle mission."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4c736909-8c67-4a04-885e-22c85ccb3900",
                                "sense_id": "61c48a22-c138-3d94-91eb-3bd902df3cf3",
                                "text": "La Convention nationale, constituée le 20 septembre 1792, ouvrit ses délibérations, et dans sa première séance abolit la royauté et proclama la république."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "17402266-77c6-4663-93b4-633be2310426",
                                "sense_id": "61c48a22-c138-3d94-91eb-3bd902df3cf3",
                                "text": "La royauté, chez vous, n'a jamais poussé que de tristes racines; votre sol républicain ne convient nullement à cet arbre-là."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "02ea4163-1129-4c0b-b47c-7f01ce8718d9",
                                "sense_id": "61c48a22-c138-3d94-91eb-3bd902df3cf3",
                                "text": "Et puis on découvrit — ce dont on aurait pu se douter à l’avance — que le rétablissement de la royauté, à la Henri V, c’est-à-dire avec son cortège d’idées désuètes et de principes périmés, était un anachronisme que la France de 1873 ne supporterait pas un instant."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9d68e710-5f5a-458e-86e4-2d0ab7f29b8b",
                                "sense_id": "61c48a22-c138-3d94-91eb-3bd902df3cf3",
                                "text": "— C'est, vous le voyez, la façon dont les Rois se tirent partout de nos jours, à cette différence près qu'à présent on évite la royauté. La royauté est si peu de mode qu'on esquive la fève par tous les moyens […]."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "3121f065-2d4c-32c3-a9b6-95975e5ef678",
                        "entry_id": "f23a9e37-c043-3571-b17a-aaf5ca1441f9",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Prééminence ; influence souveraine."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "broadly"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "33810836-ead7-4077-a8f2-77471acb8c1b",
                                "sense_id": "3121f065-2d4c-32c3-a9b6-95975e5ef678",
                                "text": "Henri IV est le grand-père de Louis XIV, Cotton, le grand-oncle du P. la Chaise : deux royautés, deux dynasties, celle des rois, celle des confesseurs jésuites."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "60e3e414-373e-421b-8667-696c630c0208",
                        "source_entry_id": "f23a9e37-c043-3571-b17a-aaf5ca1441f9",
                        "source_sense_id": "61c48a22-c138-3d94-91eb-3bd902df3cf3",
                        "source_sense_description": "(Monarchie) Régime, pouvoir, fonction d’un roi ou d’une reine.",
                        "target_lang_word": "monarchy",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "monarchy",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fb738d75-caf9-3838-a597-97251cecaafc",
                                        "entry_id": "8ddc6feb-1fa0-3ea4-8ed5-740d70eda65e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A government in which sovereignty is embodied within a single, today usually hereditary head of state (whether as a figurehead or as a powerful ruler)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "64299203-7db8-4fdb-9293-885924109408",
                                                "sense_id": "fb738d75-caf9-3838-a597-97251cecaafc",
                                                "text": "An absolute monarchy is a monarchy where the monarch is legally the ultimate authority in all temporal matters."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "51c550e9-1a86-4173-aa0d-cd79914f50b5",
                                                "sense_id": "fb738d75-caf9-3838-a597-97251cecaafc",
                                                "text": "A constitutional monarchy is a monarchy in which the monarch's power is legally constrained, ranging from where minor concessions have been made to appease certain factions to where the monarch is a figurehead with all real power in the hands of a legislative body."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "af956d90-6f87-4edd-bb94-589a289488a0",
                                                "sense_id": "fb738d75-caf9-3838-a597-97251cecaafc",
                                                "text": "He that with ſhepheards and a litle ſpoyle,\nDurſt in diſdaine of wrong and tyrannie,\nDefend his freedome gainſt a Monarchie:\nWhat will he doe ſupported by a king?"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "94b6c5d9-d4a7-3ccc-bdb6-d4e3152be93d",
                                        "entry_id": "8ddc6feb-1fa0-3ea4-8ed5-740d70eda65e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The territory ruled over by a monarch; a kingdom."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1777486f-f965-423e-b8f0-9b79ae875a5c",
                                                "sense_id": "94b6c5d9-d4a7-3ccc-bdb6-d4e3152be93d",
                                                "text": "What scourge for perjury / Can this dark monarchy afford false Clarence?"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d1b1bb59-a340-347a-a496-fb494dd409e7",
                                        "entry_id": "8ddc6feb-1fa0-3ea4-8ed5-740d70eda65e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A form of government where sovereignty is embodied by a single ruler in a state and his high aristocracy representing their separate divided lands within the state and their low aristocracy representing their separate divided fiefs."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d61afede-0911-3fca-915e-96d8e647f69b",
                                        "entry_id": "8ddc6feb-1fa0-3ea4-8ed5-740d70eda65e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "States based on a system of governance headed by a king or a queen."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "a7be6b2b-c3de-4c8d-97c8-39a6f44a15a5",
                        "source_entry_id": "f23a9e37-c043-3571-b17a-aaf5ca1441f9",
                        "source_sense_id": "61c48a22-c138-3d94-91eb-3bd902df3cf3",
                        "source_sense_description": "(Monarchie) Régime, pouvoir, fonction d’un roi ou d’une reine.",
                        "target_lang_word": "kingship",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "kingship",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b848bfd8-3d42-3658-8380-6634f1f36349",
                                        "entry_id": "8e4550bd-2ff9-3163-81bd-73c3c796f973",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The dignity, rank, or office of a king; the state of being a king."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0a6e3e16-7b04-4787-81c8-463bc83f6658",
                                                "sense_id": "b848bfd8-3d42-3658-8380-6634f1f36349",
                                                "text": "Near-synonym: kingdom"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e9158164-5fa9-4c3d-b180-d3b7a58a3c0b",
                                                "sense_id": "b848bfd8-3d42-3658-8380-6634f1f36349",
                                                "text": "The traditional world knew divine kingship."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c698dff0-4276-4c38-b746-2ecea44eb31f",
                                                "sense_id": "b848bfd8-3d42-3658-8380-6634f1f36349",
                                                "text": "[Of Henry I, who reigned 1100–1135:] Although the king's harsh treatment of his brother [Robert Curthose] sparked widespread criticism, it was typical of Henry's pragmatic approach to kingship. If he had shown greater mercy and set Robert free, it would have been only a matter of time before Curthose made fresh trouble. As it was, the Anglo-Norman territory that had been so hard won by their father was now firmly under Henry's control."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8e6de222-1f7d-3cf8-89be-cc627468b440",
                                        "entry_id": "8e4550bd-2ff9-3163-81bd-73c3c796f973",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A monarchy."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0c809f0e-0d1e-3bef-975b-cbb818487200",
                                        "entry_id": "8e4550bd-2ff9-3163-81bd-73c3c796f973",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The territory or dominion of a king; a kingdom."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
